    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The create endpoint lives in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2192 `createOwner(...)`.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`). Enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`.\n2. **Bean Validation of the `@Valid OwnerFieldsDto` body** (interface is `@Validated`). Per-field constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max=10)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max=255)`\n   - (`postcode` has no bean-validation; checked later in code)\n   \n   Failures \u2192 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`.\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` header was sent and already seen, returns the previously-created owner with **200 OK** (no creation happens).\n\n## The `createOwner` pipeline (exact order)\n\n**Validations / normalizations (each throws a mapped 4xx on failure):**\n\n4. **`addressFormNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 reconciles structured `addressLine1/2` vs flat `address` (structured wins), then trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, etc.). *Mutates the DTO.*\n5. **`ownerRequestValidator.validate`** \u2014 required-field check (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400).\n6. **`postcodeValidator.validate`** \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits and within the city's region range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n7. **`cityOwnerLimitValidator.validate`** \u2014 rejects if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` (409).\n8. **`registrationDateValidator.validate`** \u2014 rejects a future registration date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n9. **`dailyOwnerLimitValidator.validate`** \u2014 rolls to a business day; rejects if \u2265 100 owners registered that day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429).\n10. **`telephoneNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 converts to E.164 (default +61, strips formatting, drops leading 0, length checks) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). *Written back to DTO.*\n11. **`emailNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 blank \u2192 null, else regex-check and lower-case \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400). *Written back to DTO.*\n12. **`disposableEmailDomainValidator.validate`** \u2014 rejects blocklisted disposable domains (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n**Mapping + derived-field side-effects (mutating the `Owner` before save):**\n\n13. **`ownerMapper.toOwner`** \u2014 MapStruct DTO\u2192entity (ignores `id`, `pets`).\n14. **`householdIdGenerator.generate`** \u2014 sets `householdId` (SHA-256 over lastName + postcode).\n15. **Duplicate handling:**\n    - If `sharesHousehold=true`: sets `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`.\n    - Otherwise: **`duplicateOwnerValidator.validate`** \u2014 hard reject if an existing non-deleted owner shares the identity key (telephone|email|Soundex(lastName)) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409); then **`possibleDuplicateDetector`** sets soft-match `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` flags.\n16. **`memberIdGenerator.generate`** \u2014 sets `memberId` (region+FY+hash+Luhn, de-duped).\n17. **`clinicService.countNamesakes`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount`.\n18. **`householdSizeCalculator.size`** \u2014 sets `householdSize`.\n19. **`membershipLevelCapCalculator.cap`** \u2014 sets `membershipLevelCap`.\n\n**Persistence + post-save side-effects:**\n\n20. **`@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()`** (JPA callback on the entity) \u2014 sets `registrationDate` to the effective business-day date.\n21. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (`@Transactional`).\n22. **Idempotency remember** \u2014 if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id`.\n23. **`ownerAuditLogger.created`** \u2014 writes a JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (with sequence) to the AUDIT log.\n24. **`welcomeNotifier.welcome`** \u2014 writes a welcome line to the NOTIFY log.\n25. **Response build** \u2014 201 Created with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header; `toOwnerDto` additionally stamps derived response flags `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **No single transaction wraps creation.** `createOwner` is not `@Transactional`; only the individual `saveOwner`/count/find service calls are. The many uniqueness/limit checks (`findAll`, counts) and the final `save` run in separate transactions, so the \u226550-city, \u2265100-daily, and hard-duplicate checks are **subject to race conditions** under concurrent requests.\n- **Uniqueness is enforced in Java over `findAll()`**, not by a DB constraint \u2014 the duplicate, member-id, and household lookups each load all owners into memory.\n- **Entity-level constraints on `Owner`** (`@NotEmpty`, the E.164 `@Pattern`, etc.) are *not* actively triggered on this path \u2014 the `Owner` is not re-validated with `@Valid` before save; only the DTO constraints and the imperative validators gate the request.\n- The audit/notify steps run **after** save but outside its transaction, so a failure there wouldn't roll back the created owner."
